acsimile rights remain unresolved; this decision reaches only the identified complete chant.","locator":"Pustet Ratisbon1862 printedp.433, whole artifactpage519, right middle under Alleluia; checked transcriptionline1","source_ids":["artifact.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-10-29.late-marian-two-chants-projection-20261029","artifact.catholic-church.missale-romanum.pustet-ratisbon-1862.late-marian-two-chants-pages-20261029"],"status":"permitted","surfaces":["cli","corpus-data","download","print","public-git","web"]},"reason":null,"text_sha256":"50b574bde0deaf93c79d5be03e35a2d04633b2bfd731f2862b74bc2b69551b68","withheld":false},"name":"Alleluia","ordinary_disposition":{"basis":"The controlling 1962 Missal, artifact pp. 597-598, explicitly prints this chant under its seasonal heading.","group":"own-paschal-alleluia","kind":"conditional","when":{"fact":"roman-1962-common-chant-regime","in":["paschal"]}},"source":"composed","taken_from":null,"text":"Alleluia, alleluia. V. De quacumque tribulatione clamaverint ad me, exaudiam eos, et ero protector eorum semper. Alleluia. V. Fac nos innocuam, Joseph, decurrere vitam: sitque tuo semper tuta patrocinio. Alleluia.\n","text_status":null,"translations":[{"caution":"Original study translation; not approved for liturgical use or recitation.","lang":"en","rights":"project-created","source_label":"Triptych study English","text":"Alleluia, alleluia. V. From whatever distress they cry to me, I will hear them, and I will always be their protector. Alleluia. V. Joseph, grant us to lead an innocent life, and may it always be safe under your protection. Alleluia.\n"}],"unavailable_translations":null,"untranslated":null},{"citations":[{"book":"Matthew","loci":{"hebrew":[{"chapter":13,"first":54,"last":58}],"hebrew-unnumbered-titles":[{"chapter":13,"first":54,"last":58}],"vulgate":[{"chapter":13,"first":54,"last":58}]},"ref":"Matthew 13:54-58","token":"Matt","unresolved":null}],"coverage":{"c